-    <div class="gr-section">
-      <div class="gr-section-head">
-        <div>
-          <h2>Compiler acceptance gates</h2>
-          <p>Deterministic evidence needed before a person downloads the two files.</p>
-        </div>
-      </div>
-      <div class="table-responsive">
-        <table class="table table-sm">
-          <thead><tr><th>Gate</th><th>Pass condition</th></tr></thead>
-          <tbody>
-            <tr><td>Same cohort</td><td>RIS and SAMPLE reference the same immutable accepted-record snapshot and scope profile</td></tr>
-            <tr><td>Completeness</td><td>Required dimensions are present; unavailable values use the WHO-defined unknown code</td></tr>
-            <tr><td>Negatives</td><td>No-growth specimens remain in SAMPLE and never fabricate an isolate in RIS</td></tr>
-            <tr><td>Repeat isolates</td><td>One centrally configured rule runs once against cross-site patient identity</td></tr>
-            <tr><td>Traceability</td><td>Every aggregate count drills back to contributing canonical records and their source rows/resources</td></tr>
-            <tr><td>Privacy</td><td>Names and direct identifiers are absent from aggregate output; access to line-level evidence is controlled</td></tr>
-            <tr><td>Reproducibility</td><td>Same data snapshot + mappings + standards + GLASS profile produces byte-identical outputs</td></tr>
-            <tr><td>Human release</td><td>Named authorized reviewer records validation and manually uploads to WHO</td></tr>
-          </tbody>
-        </table>
-      </div>
-    </div>
