-      <div class="gr-section-head">
-        <div>
-          <h2>Current OpenELIS implementation</h2>
-          <p>Observed in the deployed AMR code: useful foundations exist, but the current export is not a GLASS replacement.</p>
-        </div>
-      </div>
-      <div class="table-responsive">
-        <table class="table table-sm">
-          <thead><tr><th>Capability</th><th>Observed state</th><th>Assessment</th><th>Required move</th></tr></thead>
-          <tbody>
-            <tr><td>FHIR R4 transport</td><td>Configurable subscriptions/export for Patient, Specimen, ServiceRequest, Observation, DiagnosticReport</td><td><span class="viz-badge gr-status-good">Reuse</span></td><td>Add a structured microbiology profile and transformation</td></tr>
-            <tr><td>Microbiology source data</td><td>Cases, isolates, reviewed AST readings, methods, interpretations, release states</td><td><span class="viz-badge gr-status-good">Reuse</span></td><td>Project atomic microbiology content into FHIR</td></tr>
-            <tr><td>Patient report projection</td><td>Culture is flattened into one remark value with a 200-character limit</td><td><span class="viz-badge gr-status-bad">Insufficient</span></td><td>Keep human report text, add structured culture/isolate/AST observations</td></tr>
-            <tr><td>Current “WHONET” output</td><td>15-column identifiable CSV, one row per reviewed AST reading</td><td><span class="viz-badge gr-status-warn">Prototype only</span></td><td>Do not evolve it into GLASS; feed canonical records to a separate compiler</td></tr>
-            <tr><td>Negative cultures</td><td>AST-driven export excludes cases with no isolate/readings</td><td><span class="viz-badge gr-status-bad">Missing denominator</span></td><td>Send finalized no-growth specimen outcomes through FHIR/canonical ingest</td></tr>
-            <tr><td>Mapping targets</td><td>Organisms and antibiotics carry WHONET codes; breakpoint import refers to antibiotic WHONET code</td><td><span class="viz-badge gr-status-bad">Dependency leak</span></td><td>Canonical concepts first; WHONET codes become optional aliases</td></tr>
-            <tr><td>First-isolate logic</td><td>Facility export can de-duplicate in 7/14/30-day windows</td><td><span class="viz-badge gr-status-warn">Wrong layer for GLASS</span></td><td>Send complete line-level records; perform GLASS repeat logic nationally</td></tr>
-            <tr><td>General file import</td><td>No BacLink-equivalent CSV/XLSX mapping and saved profile flow</td><td><span class="viz-badge gr-status-bad">Missing</span></td><td>Build source-layout profiles, code mapping, preview, quarantine, rerun</td></tr>
-            <tr><td>GLASS compiler</td><td>No versioned RIS/SAMPLE aggregate generator</td><td><span class="viz-badge gr-status-bad">Missing</span></td><td>Build in the national report application, not the facility LIS</td></tr>
-          </tbody>
