-    <div class="gr-section">
-      <div class="gr-section-head">
-        <div>
-          <h2>Functional mock drift to correct</h2>
-          <p>OpenELIS Work remains the functional design source, but two WHONET assumptions now contradict the stated replacement goal and WHO reporting semantics.</p>
-        </div>
-      </div>
-      <div class="table-responsive">
-        <table class="table table-sm">
-          <thead><tr><th>Mock statement</th><th>Problem</th><th>Product-safe correction</th></tr></thead>
-          <tbody>
-            <tr class="gr-drift"><td>“Each local code resolves to a WHONET code”</td><td>Makes WHONET's vocabulary the internal target</td><td>Resolve to a canonical concept and its WHO GLASS output code; retain WHONET as an optional alias for legacy import</td></tr>
-            <tr class="gr-drift"><td>“WHONET file upload” as the non-OpenELIS route</td><td>Still requires sites to run WHONET/BacLink</td><td>Offer general line-level CSV/XLSX upload with a saved import profile; also accept WHONET files for migration compatibility</td></tr>
-            <tr class="gr-drift"><td>RIS described as “per isolate”</td><td>WHO defines RIS submission data as aggregate R/I/S counts across required strata</td><td>Show contributing isolate count separately; label output rows as aggregate GLASS records</td></tr>
-            <tr><td>National first-isolate selection</td><td>Aligned with cross-site de-duplication need</td><td>Keep; require privacy-safe patient matching and full line-level ingest</td></tr>
-            <tr><td>Manual focal-point upload</td><td>Aligned with current product boundary</td><td>Keep; record download, review, upload date, and output version</td></tr>
-          </tbody>
-        </table>
-      </div>
-    </div>
