-  <section class="gr-panel" id="gr-panel-decisions" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="gr-tab-decisions" data-gr-panel="decisions" hidden>
-    <div class="gr-section">
-      <div class="gr-section-head">
-        <div>
-          <h2>Architecture decisions</h2>
-          <p>Recommended defaults separate confirmed product direction from decisions that need explicit validation.</p>
-        </div>
-      </div>
-
-      <div class="gr-decision">
-        <div><strong>Application boundary</strong><span class="viz-badge gr-status-good">Recommended</span></div>
-        <div>Separate national reporting application consuming multiple laboratories; OpenELIS remains a facility data producer.</div>
-        <div class="text-small">Prevents GLASS-specific aggregation and national identity logic from distorting routine LIS workflows.</div>
-      </div>
-      <div class="gr-decision">
-        <div><strong>Open profile format</strong><span class="viz-badge gr-status-good">Recommended</span></div>
-        <div>UI-authored, versioned JSON or YAML profile with parser settings, field rules, dictionaries, validation policy, and tests.</div>
-        <div class="text-small">Exportable and reviewable; not a WHONET <code>.cfg</code> clone.</div>
-      </div>
-      <div class="gr-decision">
-        <div><strong>Clinical interpretation</strong><span class="viz-badge gr-status-good">Recommended</span></div>
-        <div>Preserve reviewed site interpretation. When only raw AST exists, compute from explicitly selected CLSI/EUCAST version; retain both source and computed values.</div>
-        <div class="text-small">No silent standard mixing; direct CLSI use requires licensed distribution or site-supplied data.</div>
-      </div>
-      <div class="gr-decision">
-        <div><strong>Canonical terminology</strong><span class="viz-badge gr-status-good">Recommended</span></div>
-        <div>Internal stable concepts with aliases for local, WHO GLASS, FHIR terminology, and optional WHONET codes.</div>
-        <div class="text-small">Avoids replacing one tool-specific coupling with another brittle transport coupling.</div>
-      </div>
-      <div class="gr-decision">
-        <div><strong>National patient matching</strong><span class="viz-badge gr-status-warn">Needs design</span></div>
-        <div>Choose a privacy-preserving, stable cross-site patient key and define collision/absence handling.</div>
-        <div class="text-small">Without it, national repeat-isolate selection cannot be correct across facilities.</div>
-      </div>
-      <div class="gr-decision">
-        <div><strong>Current GLASS contract</strong><span class="viz-badge gr-status-warn">Needs source fixture</span></div>
-        <div>Obtain the active WHO templates/data dictionary and freeze them as a versioned compiler profile with official validation examples.</div>
-        <div class="text-small">Do not infer current file columns from old WHONET output or mock labels.</div>
-      </div>
-      <div class="gr-decision">
-        <div><strong>Replacement scope</strong><span class="viz-badge gr-status-info">Proposed boundary</span></div>
-        <div>Eliminate WHONET from the GLASS submission path; preserve optional compatibility imports. Local outbreak analytics and every WHONET analysis screen are separate product scope.</div>
-        <div class="text-small">Keeps the deliverable testable while removing operational dependence for national reporting.</div>
-      </div>
-    </div>
-
-    <div class="gr-section">
-      <div class="gr-section-head">
-        <div>
-          <h2>Manageable build order</h2>
-          <p>Each slice has a visible, testable exit condition.</p>
-        </div>
-      </div>
-      <ol class="gr-roadmap">
-        <li><div><strong>Freeze external contracts</strong><span class="text-small">Acquire current WHO RIS/SAMPLE templates, representative FHIR bundles, real wide/long site files, a WHONET isolate file, and authorized CLSI/EUCAST fixtures. Exit: golden inputs and expected outputs are review-approved.</span></div></li>
-        <li><div><strong>Canonical model + lineage</strong><span class="text-small">Implement specimens, culture outcomes, isolates, AST, terminology aliases, import runs, and source pointers. Exit: positives, negatives, amendments, and multiple isolates round-trip without loss.</span></div></li>
-        <li><div><strong>Open mapping profile</strong><span class="text-small">Define portable profile schema and execution engine. Exit: same file + profile produces identical canonical records; incompatible headers block before import.</span></div></li>
-        <li><div><strong>CSV / Excel workbench</strong><span class="text-small">Add sheet/header/delimiter/encoding, wide/long AST, code frequencies, preview, map/ignore/block, quarantine, and rerun. Exit: a non-OpenELIS site completes a recurring import without WHONET.</span></div></li>
-        <li><div><strong>Structured OpenELIS FHIR</strong><span class="text-small">Publish culture, no growth, isolate, and AST observations through existing transport. Exit: national ingest reconstructs the same canonical record as the facility case.</span></div></li>
-        <li><div><strong>Standards interpretation service</strong><span class="text-small">Load versioned CLSI/EUCAST data legally, retain raw/source/computed values, and explain every result. Exit: a published conformance set matches expected S/I/R behavior.</span></div></li>
-        <li><div><strong>National scope + repeat logic</strong><span class="text-small">Apply period, subset, specimen/pathogen eligibility, patient matching, and current GLASS repeat policy once. Exit: cross-site repeats and no-growth denominators pass worked examples.</span></div></li>
-        <li><div><strong>RIS + SAMPLE compiler</strong><span class="text-small">Generate versioned outputs, quality report, traceable counts, review sign-off, and run history. Exit: official validator accepts both files and every aggregate cell traces to inputs.</span></div></li>
-        <li><div><strong>Operational qualification</strong><span class="text-small">Accessibility, performance, security, backup/recovery, mapping governance, staged rollout, and UAT. Exit: representative national volume and failure recovery are demonstrated.</span></div></li>
-      </ol>
-    </div>
-
-    <div class="gr-section">
-      <div class="gr-section-head">
-        <div>
-          <h2>Non-negotiable acceptance criteria</h2>
-          <p>These are the replacement test, not visual similarity to WHONET.</p>
-        </div>
-      </div>
-      <div class="table-responsive">
-        <table class="table table-sm">
-          <thead><tr><th>Area</th><th>Deterministic criterion</th></tr></thead>
-          <tbody>
-            <tr><td>Profile reuse</td><td>A profile created from one source layout imports a later matching file without remapping; drift blocks with an exact diff</td></tr>
-            <tr><td>Structural coverage</td><td>CSV/XLSX, wide and long AST, one/multiple rows per isolate, and disk/MIC/Etest examples reach equivalent canonical records</td></tr>
-            <tr><td>Unknowns</td><td>Every unmapped code has kind, source, frequency, affected rows, and explicit disposition; no row disappears silently</td></tr>
-            <tr><td>FHIR parity</td><td>The same laboratory case ingested by FHIR and tabular import normalizes to equivalent specimen/isolate/AST meaning</td></tr>
-            <tr><td>Standards</td><td>Every computed interpretation identifies authority, version, rule inputs, and result; reviewed source interpretation remains visible</td></tr>
-            <tr><td>Denominator</td><td>Finalized no-growth records contribute to SAMPLE even though they produce no RIS isolate</td></tr>
-            <tr><td>De-duplication</td><td>Cross-site repeats are evaluated once at national level against a versioned policy and privacy-safe patient identity</td></tr>
-            <tr><td>GLASS output</td><td>RIS and SAMPLE pass the current official validation fixture and derive from one immutable cohort</td></tr>
-            <tr><td>Auditability</td><td>Any output count can be explained from aggregate cell → canonical records → source rows/resources → profile and code decisions</td></tr>
-            <tr><td>Independence</td><td>A clean deployment with no WHONET software or data tables can ingest, contextualize, interpret, aggregate, validate, and export</td></tr>
-          </tbody>
-        </table>
-      </div>
-    </div>
-  </section>
